# Paths whose privacy-check hits are deliberate and acknowledged.
#
# Safe to commit, and committed on purpose: this file names PATHS, never
# personal data, so it can be reviewed by anyone who can see the repo. That
# is the opposite of .privacy-tokens, which holds the identifiers themselves
# and must stay gitignored.
#
# An allowlisted path is excluded from the exit code but still printed in
# the report, marked as allowlisted. Nothing here disappears — allowlisting
# is by path, so a file on this list could later gain a token nobody
# intended, and the hit staying visible is what keeps that honest.
#
# One path per line, relative to the repo root. Write the reason above the
# entry. A missing entry is a failing run, which is the right default.

